.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt INTERFACES 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm interfaces
.Nd inspect current NIC state and enumerated Ethernet controllers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Query the kernel directly for selected driver, PCI identity, MAC, current
carrier and disabled state, acquisition ticks and receive/transmit counters.
Enumerate Ethernet-class PCI functions, identifying the selected function
and inactive functions whose admission state is unknown.
No network or file-server transaction is needed to acquire these facts.
The command never sends a packet, enables a device or clears quarantine.
.Pp
Speed, duplex and physical jack mapping remain unknown when not established.
Carrier down does not prove a missing cable, and carrier up does not prove
peer reachability. A failed or disabled reading never preserves an earlier
up indication. Driver failure reasons remain in
.Xr dmesg 1 .
Address and route configuration are separately available from
.Xr net-status 1 ,
whose retained sample has an explicit age.
.Pp
This development interface requires an inherited read-only diagnostics capability.
It grants no raw NIC, process-control or machine-control right.
If the driver cannot supply a counter sample, RX and TX counts are unknown;
an unavailable sample is not reported as a measurement of zero.
.Pp
Device queries require UP/BSP execution.
On an application processor, the command reports
.Dq unsupported
and exits with status 1 without accessing the device.
The diagnostic grant does not pin all operator commands to the BSP.
This version makes no SMP interface-availability claim.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 for complete readout, 1 for an unavailable query, 2 for invalid arguments.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr net-status 1 ,
.Xr sysinfo 1 ,
.Xr ps 1
